# IaC Agent — Technical Documentation

---

## Page 1: Overview & Architecture

### 1.1 What is it?

**IaC Agent** is an AI-powered Infrastructure as Code generation platform that converts natural language descriptions of cloud infrastructure into production-ready IaC configurations. It uses a **ReAct (Reason + Act) agent** pattern built on LangChain, backed by a pluggable LLM abstraction layer supporting **Azure OpenAI**, **Google Gemini**, and **OpenAI**.

The system features a **Generate → Validate → Fix** loop: it generates IaC code, runs it against a comprehensive policy engine, and auto-remediates any security or compliance violations — all from a single chat prompt.

### 1.2 Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology | Details |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| **Frontend** | Vite + React (JSX) | Chat UI with TailwindCSS, Lucide icons |
| **Backend** | FastAPI (Python) | REST API with CORS, Pydantic models |
| **Agent Framework** | LangChain (ReAct) | `hwchase17/react` prompt template |
| **LLM Providers** | Azure OpenAI / Gemini / OpenAI | Pluggable via `LLM_PROVIDER` env var |
| **Output Format** | Terraform / Kubernetes / Ansible / Docker Compose | Auto-detected from content |

